A³-X00TD 4.19.x Kernel Source
=============================

Getting Started
---------------
To use this kernel source for building rom, you need clone with this command
```bash
git clone --single-branch --recursive https://github.com/aepranata/kernel_asus_X00TD.git kernel/asus/X00TD
```

To use this kernel source for standalone compile, you need clone with this command
```bash
git clone --single-branch --recursive https://github.com/aepranata/kernel_asus_X00TD.git <kernel-path>
```


KernelSU-Next
--------
KernelSU-Next is implemented and enabled by default. If u don't want it, Do this:

Add this into boot cmdline
```bash
kernelsu.enabled=0
```

Or, Disable this config
```bash
CONFIG_KSU
```

If u only want to enable Safe Mode (U should enable KernelSU too), Which u just want Root Access and Modules Feature disabled, Do this:

Add this into boot cmdline
```bash
kernelsu.safemode=1
```

Or, Set this in defconfig.
```bash
CONFIG_KSU_SAFE_MODE=y
```

Source: https://github.com/aepranata/KernelSU-Next


Using New Novatek Touchscreen Driver
------------------------------------
This source is still using original driver from 4.4 source... but, i have updated nvt driver.

Working smoothly on mine with new driver.

If u want to use new driver, do this:

Add this into boot cmdline. Or
```bash
use_new_nvtouch=1
```

Or, Hardcode, set this to 1
```bash
https://github.com/RyuujiX/android_kernel_asus_sdm660-4.19/blob/test/init/main.c#L147
```

Or, Disable Original NVT Driver in defconfig. `CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_NT36xxx_ASUS` is New NVT Driver.
